  <h1>Jersey City Was Drinking Its Own Sewage</h1>
  <p class="dek">In 1896 typhoid killed 85 people out of every 100,000 in Jersey City. The fix arrived in 1908, done in secret, and the man behind it could have gone to prison for it.</p>
